    i "One year ago, Shiroya and I finished high school together. In Yushibana, people tended to move out if they planned to attend university, seeing as the closest one was hours away. That was why we hadn't yet decided on what to do and thought of the year 2011 as a pivotal point where we'd decide. Money wasn't an immediate problem for either of us, and we weren't sure what we wanted to study if we decided to move."
    i "The last important factor that influenced our decision first made an appearance in our lives when we started middle school. Most of us were the same people who had attended elementary school together, but a new classmate named Miiya moved to Yushibana that year."
    i "At first, Shiroya and I didn't talk to her much, and neither did our usual group of friends. Miiya quickly became comfortable with other people in our class, which kept some distance between us."
    nvl clear
    with dissolve
    i "That changed three years later, the day she approached me when I was alone. She was curious about us and wanted to hang out. I never really understood what drove her to do that, but we spent an entire afternoon together, and following that day, she would spend some time with me every so often."
    i "A few months later, she appeared when Shiroya and I were together, and they introduced themselves in more depth. Since then, the three of us started to become comfortable around each other after school. It was out of the ordinary for us since we were used to being alone, but we quickly took a liking to Miiya.{w} She was a blunt and sincere girl—one who didn't seem to have many worries in life or think too hard about things. Even though she'd made her way into our lives out of the blue, we became accustomed to her presence."
    i "Initially, she passed the time with us sporadically and acted as another link between Shiroya and me, but the frequency increased to the point where the three of us would spend almost every afternoon together."
