    i "While the person responsible had to be around us, it was possible they hadn't thought of it yet. Since Erina and Shiroya had heard the recording, I found it unlikely either of them would be the one to eventually cause that outcome. If they did, their idea of staying for one more month would've originally come from hearing the recording, just like how I'd thought of some of its benefits only because the idea had been presented to me. A causal loop like that, generating an idea from nothing, still sounded irrational to me."
    i "Sai was the one who first presented the draft of a theory I was using—that the time the Sekimeiya spent outside of its cabinet was what determined the amount of time traveled.{w} If that was the fundamental motive of our extended imprisonment, Sai was the best candidate to suspect. He had never listened to the audio. However, that same recording also made it sound as if we'd been abandoned by the world outside, so it was potentially foolish to blame someone in the building instead."
    nvl clear
