    i "But the reality was that we were most likely still sharing space with a murderer who had killed anywhere from one to three times. The death of the second Naomi had almost certainly been a normal homicide, but I wasn't sure if the case was the same with Isla.{w} The culprit's actions had been linked to the Sekimeiya from the beginning, and they had managed to escape us so far. It was strange how they'd known about the Sekimeiya's powers straight away, and it had begun to seem like they were from the far future."
    i "...We could all easily have been in the middle of their process.{w} All of us had learned about the Sekimeiya's powers. Then, someone decided to trap us for an entire month and would actually accomplish it somehow.{w} In the future, once the required time passed, they would travel back and exist at the start of the day's events with a full understanding of the Sekimeiya."
    i "They would cause what they'd once seen, which meant that at that moment, a future version of one of us existed somewhere. It was a bit paradoxical too, but depending on how they would replicate the events they'd experienced, it might've made sense.{w} It was like the first time I'd traveled to the past, when Shiroya hadn't realized that I was from the future.{w} What if we had already found the culprit in one of our searches but didn't realize it? Could they have impersonated their past self at some point?"
