    n "Even though this is an extreme situation, it can apply in any circumstance because it removes the generalized risk associated with going back to the past.{w} Regardless of the circumstances, you can think something up in your head. If it'll work, you'll see the successful result, and if it won't, nothing will happen. You would be guaranteed to never fail, no matter what you attempt.{w} The killer could've used this method before killing Naomi; \"if I move this specific way after killing her and I'm not seen, I'll let my current self know by leaving a drawer in the next room open\", for example."
    n "Another big advantage is that you'd be able to make any move that's currently hard to accomplish by deciding it to occur retroactively.{w} At some point, the killer might have wanted to prevent us from entering a room. However, they couldn't go and lock it, or they would've been seen."
