    i "Just as I'd been fond of Atsuki since years in the past, I'd never liked her constant presence. The me from two weeks earlier had shrugged off her disappearance, and the me stuck in the tower couldn't even care about her imminent return. It was all tiresome."
    i "Coming to the exhibit had ironically worked to bring her back, and it might've been for the better. Even though Atsuki had offered for me to stay with him temporarily, I'd never been sure he would have recovered without going to live with his parents."
    i "We had to accept we were leaving many questions behind, but there were plenty more in the outside world. Perhaps it wasn't a bad idea to consider finding a job somewhere else if I had the chance. I'd recently learned how much I despised acting differently than I felt, which was bound to persist if I didn't."
