     #actually i'm going to go into a bit more depth here. maybe we will even put this in a tip later. GSM was the 2G network standard in much of the world, but in japan, it was PDC for quite some time. PDC was phased out formally in march of 2012; for GSM networks, they actually required the user to input the time manually (they could not pull it from a network) unless they had a GPS chip. obviously GSM is not the same as PDC, but the point here is that there wasn't a necessarily widespread standard of automatic time updates until 3G and later in some areas of the world, so all that really needs to be said here is that shiroya was still on a (fictional, please no sue me) PDC network which did not offer automatic time updates at this time and after march would have been on 3G
