    c "It wasn't a secret that a large portion of the citizens was opposed to the presence Ashiya had built. Due to Ashiya Tower, Yushibana had undergone a drastic change throughout the recent years."
    c "Perhaps the old activities of what had once been called the Ashiya family weren't as widely known, but what was a commonly shared fact was that when the tower had shifted into a personal exposition center, a new wave of people had taken over the town."
    c "That was the fundamental dispute in Yushibana. The older citizens, aware of the way Ashiya had once been, were becoming outnumbered by the recent influx of people Ashiya had brought, who supported the now-corporation due to financial reasons and were ignorant of its roots.{w} After the 15th of December, the backlash Ashiya had received had been enormous. Through their poor security measures, they'd let two people be killed, and they hadn't publicly responded well to the ordeal, blinded by their battle against Xyn."
    c "Unlike previously, the protests were so strong and visible that the supportive part of Yushibana joined in as well. Everything Ashiya had done to combat Xyn was being revealed, so the older citizens took the chance to expose all they knew about Ashiya's past, and rumors about the missing people and the unknown gas continued to circulate."
    nvl clear
    with dissolve
    $ Pause(0.5)
    c "All Ashiya kept saying was that they were still investigating what had happened—that they would find the missing people and expose those working as part of Xyn. Then, the tower would quickly open again.{w} However, everyone knew that nobody had entered that building since the 15th due to the unknown gas, so those statements were seen as a haphazard, lacking defense."
    c "Where were the remaining people? Why had they not been in the tower?{w} One of them had died in a car accident, and another one had been unable to explain anything to the police. It didn't make sense; they should've been in the tower, late on the 15th. ...And what about the other three? They hadn't been found anywhere."
