    c "That began to shine a bit of light on the situation. The demolition of the tower was something one part of Yushibana had always wished for. The structure that clearly didn't belong with the others—the one they'd all seen rapidly increasing in height throughout the years..."
    c "Why had it been purchased just to be demolished? Had it been to follow that old, unattainable demand that Ashiya disappear? Did they hope the rumors still tied with that building would vanish so that something entirely new could be built? There was only speculation on those topics throughout Yushibana, and nothing more."
    $ Pause(0.5)
    nvl clear
    show bg black
    with dissolve
    $ Pause(3.0)
    show bg cg1-4
    with dissolve
    c "Weeks had passed, but any answers remained staunchly concealed. However, a date had already been appointed: on October 4th, the building would be destroyed."
    c "It was a tall and wide structure, so demolishing it wasn't simple. As no buildings were directly next to it, though, there was little danger to any of the surroundings."
    c "At some point, the unanswered questions had almost faded. Who had caused the incident on the 15th of December? Who had killed the two victims? Where were the remaining people? Given the blood that had been found, the worst had been assumed by all."
