    with dissolve
    c "After so long, there was a reason why Shiroya and her cat had their heads out their window.{w} It was October 4th, and the sight they were beholding would no longer exist the following day."
    c "In the distance, the building stretching past the others was soon to fall. It could've been dangerous to get close to it, so many people were also watching from within their houses. Some of them were about to have a familiar view returned to them. Others, like Shiroya, could hardly imagine what a Yushibana without Ashiya Tower would be like."
    c "At {time=12}, the demolition would begin. There'd been no correspondence from Ashiya in months. The facts behind the unknown gas and the deaths within the tower were still shrouded in darkness.{w} The interior of the building had been investigated a few times after the 15th, but nothing useful had been figured out. Ashiya had removed everything of value, so after it was verified by the new owner, the demolition seemed to pose no risk aside from the dust it would scatter across the hill behind the tower."
    #i dont say whether its am or pm (its pm) because in umineko the bomb goes off at 12 am which the demolition symbolizes oh well - nevermind shoutouts to time format options
    c "A minute before the appointed time, many pairs of eyes looked on from behind windows all over town."
