    with dissolve
    c "She'd set the volume low because the sporadic static would be hard on her ears otherwise."
    c "..."
    c "The bright screen projected light onto the ceiling. When the color drastically changed, Shiroya lifted her head."
    snn "..."
    $ Pause(0.3)
    snn "...!"
    c "She raised her entire body next. On the screen was a man speaking into a microphone.{w} She grabbed the remote and increased the volume, staring at the text beneath him."
    c "She had to read it a few times to comprehend it."
    show bg tv2
    nvl clear
    with dissolve
    c "\"The last three people who were trapped in Ashiya Tower found dead\"."
    c "In the corner of the screen was an image of the piled debris. Shiroya focused her hearing and began to process the deep voice of the reporter."
    nn "...en they started to be removed, the first body was found. It was that of Akaro Esata."
    c "A video began to play in the background. It showed people removing the debris and a pixelated red blob in the middle."
    nn "Another one was quickly found afterward, belonging to Sai Yomiya. Finally, when almost all the debris had been removed, Erina Majutsu's body was found.{w} The three bodies were heavily crushed, and it's believed some parts of them weren't found."
    #erina's body is after the others because it was in the mechanical room whereas the first two were in the entrance
    c "Shiroya listened in disbelief. She'd always known that when she'd touched the Sekimeiya, Atsuki, Erina, Sai, and Akaro had been in the lobby. Atsuki had died in a car accident, but the others had all disappeared. A long time ago, Shiroya had concluded that Atsuki must've traveled through time after her."
    c "But this... What kind of sense did it make? The censoring prevented her from confirming the bodies' faces, but given their descriptions, it didn't seem like that would've been possible regardless."
    nvl clear
    with dissolve
    $ TipOrbShow("demolition")
    nn "As of now, what happened is unknown. While the bodies were severely smashed, they were not fully decomposed. It has been determined that they died the day of the demolition.{w} However, the possibility of the demolition itself causing their deaths has been thoroughly refuted. It was properly verified that nobody was in the building before the impact, and that's not the only reason.{w} The three bodies were below all the rubble. If the building had really fallen on them, their condition would be even worse. Strangely, some of the body parts that were recovered are practically intact, despite the state of most others.{w} There was no dust discovered on the bodies—neither inside their clothes nor in their mouths. For this reason, the situation is being handled very carefully, as the truth behind it might be appalling.{w} It has been considered that the bodies were disposed of within the rubble following the demolition since they couldn't have been directly hit by it. However, given how deep they were and the absence of blood around them, that was immediately discarded as well.{w} Even though the abundance of the unidentified old gas has disappeared, around the three bodies was where the last remaining traces were found.{w} This is an extremely delicate case that has carried unsolved questions with it all year. Now that everyone who was trapped in the building has been found, the authorities will do all they can to figure out what happened on that day."
    show bg black
    $ TipOrbHide()
