    i "I would... change the past. I had a way to save Miiya, Atsuki, Isla, Katei, Naomi, Erina..."
    i "I had traveled from the 15th to change the past alone, and even though I hadn't been aware of what would happen, I had considered the outcome with my other self."
    i "..."
    i "Looking at the small town had finally brought me to lean toward an option. I'd decided to do my best to change the past, as the possible consequences didn't outweigh what good could be achieved."
    i "But the tower I could see far in the distance... I still couldn't go there."
    nvl clear
    with dissolve
    i "The day I'd enter that building again would likely be the last day of my normal life, and even though I'd decided, the thought could still freeze me in place."
    i "I wanted the days I had to persist, but that couldn't happen. My life in Yushibana was likely soon to end, and I could choose the length of the last stretch."
    i "If I saved Miiya, I wouldn't show myself to her, Atsuki, and the other me, even though I didn't know yet what I would do."
    i "So the issue to solve was the possibility of a knowledgeable enemy who could change the past on their own and steal the Sekimeiya before the 15th."
    i "I couldn't do much to combat that aside from rushing in, which I found far too risky. So I settled on another course of action and accepted that I would take it."
    i "Thursday was two days away.{w} Every Thursday morning, an event would be held in the tower. That was the day I chose to step into the building for the second time and find the Sekimeiya that was surely confined inside."
    nvl clear
    with dissolve
