    #So, for the longest time I was gonna have a credits sequence to further explain (or introduce) the structure of the three timelines. Things such as:
    #First of all, that the tower would open again in B because the remaining people were found (which should be pretty clear anyway.)
    #B was needed to reach C, however it was A what allowed B to happen (Isla A and Akaro A world splitting to B etc). In A everyone died, Atsuki was accused, and part of japan disappeared. Within the tower during the 12 hours there was no information to go off of.
    #In B some people died and some got out a while later. Akaro was arrested, but it was Akaro A, the version who most regretted what he'd done. Isla returned, but it was Isla A, who couldn't be happy about the reunion. It was however the only world where Atsuki+Shiroya got out with the Sekimeiya - the key to reach B.
    #Atsuki does call C the perfect world. Everyone who got trapped ended up alive, aside from Suripo, who was an external casualty. Erina seemed to die, but she soon revived as it had been Erina A. Atsuki+Shiroya+Miiya ended up alive, but the end of C2 does imply that might not end up as well as Atsuki thinks. Furthermore, before the end, a tragedy was very close from happening, which would've shattered everything needed to get to that point.
    #In A, some people ended up at B. In B, they briefly visited C but came back. In C, they briefly visited A and B but ended up being able to return to C. There's a bunch of stuff like Atsuki A pulling him out of C, the fact that C loops back to A (C is still "one step" close to A, the distance A and B have between each other. This goes back to the "world given to them that can be broken with a single action), Atsuki A being in B and C momentarily and then being dropped back to A through the elevator's fall, the info that Atsuki gets in C (the usb recording) is used in B to catch Akaro A on January 3rd (due to the nature of B akaro B doesn't get arrested since A already did)
    #I would imply too that the hallway formations represent the timelines. A and B are the two ways to reach C, and they're linked by the Sekimeiya in the middle.
    #I don't know if any of this is implied without reading it. If it is but is still subtle, having this in the credits might not be a good idea. However, if it's gonna come out of nowhere, maybe I would prefer to have it.
    #-------------------------------------
    #the logo of the game shouldn't be an egg because that hides the fact that there are two
    $ Pause(0.4)
    nvl clear
    with dissolve
    $ Pause(0.4)
    scene bg cg10
    with slowdissolve
    $ UnlockAllTips(1)
    $ UnlockNote("c5_013", 16)
    $ UnlockNote("c5_013", 17)
    $ Pause(5.0)
